      "description": "The DMARC record sets p=quarantine with t=y. RFC 9989 section 4.7 asks receivers to apply one level below the stated policy, so failing mail gets none. RFC 7489 receivers do not know the t tag and apply p=quarantine as written. Which happens depends on the receiver.",
      "impact": "At receivers following RFC 9989, forged mail gets none, so it is delivered.",
      "remediation": "t=y is for testing a policy before you enforce it. Once your reports show every legitimate sender passing, remove t=y (or set t=n).",
      "references": [
        "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9989#section-4.7"
      ],
